{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792412540,"nonce":"EUIQHATR/Ap0HeCkm78gziGX0JA=","title":"The dashboard hides panels in a window under 1240 by 860, and on the web the full layout fills the heap","message":"**Symptom**\nBelow 1240 by 860 layout units the Vehicle page dropped four of its six panels (battery, tyres, energy, chargers), and below 900 by 560 all of them. A window of at least that size on the web froze between page changes with the music playing on: the page stopped drawing and the collector ran over a hundred times a lap, `origin=large-exhaustion freed=0`, at about 380 MB live.\n\n**Layout**\nThe pages are laid out for at least 1160 by 880 units; a smaller window has the layout made larger than it, as a browser zoomed out is, drawn at the window's own resolution. `--ui-zoom` on `:root`, set under `@media` steps in dashboard.css (rules read the window's own size, so the zoom cannot flip with what it makes), is read by WindowedApp each frame: logical size, pointer input, the IME area and a window drag follow it. `ASHUI_ZOOM=\u003cn\u003e` pins it for scripted runs; tests/wasm/dashboard_check.mjs does, at 1. Screen.wide and Screen.medium are gone: every panel shows at every size.\n\n**Memory**\nWith all six panels the chargers panel's 316 by 100 map drew the whole street map: each visit added about 90 MB of live heap on the web (about 210 MB at the start against 133 MB with two panels), so a lap of the pages hit the heap's limit. Each experiment was a web build run through eight docks laps at 880 high: without the map, 131 MB and +5 MB a lap; with the streets alone, 216 MB and exhausted; without the credit text, 152 MB and still +75 MB a lap. The panel's map now leaves out the buildings, rails, paths, side streets and its canvas text (the credit is a text element over it): 143 MB at the start, 243 MB after eight laps, still drawing.\n\nThe cause of one canvas's cost is not found: a map this small should not need 90 MB, and canvas text and the stroke tessellation look worth a profile. The pre-existing growth of 17b4b2b may be part of it.\n\n**Also**\ntests/wasm/smoke.sh passed the seconds where dashboard_check.mjs expects the work directory, so the dashboard lane failed before it began; the check now takes `\u003curl\u003e \u003cport\u003e \u003cseconds\u003e \u003cwork\u003e`.","files":null}]}